WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.561
day I wanted to see Mr.

2
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:18.483
Rochester, but I feared seeing him too.

3
00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:23.427
I wanted to hear his voice again, yet I feared meeting his eye.

4
00:00:24.428 --> 00:00:27.330
During the morning I was sure he would visit the schoolroom.

5
00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:34.036
But the morning passed as usual, and no one arrived to interrupt the quiet course of Adele's studies.

6
00:00:35.164 --> 00:00:38.086
At one point I heard some bustle in the vicinity of Mr.

7
00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:39.307
Rochester's bedroom.

8
00:00:39.327 --> 00:00:43.430
"What a blessing that our master was not burned in his bed!"

9
00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:44.731
exclaimed Leah.

10
00:00:45.692 --> 00:00:49.835
"How fortunate that he had the presence of mind to think of the water jug!"

11
00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:50.735
said Mrs.

12
00:00:50.795 --> 00:00:55.399
Fairfax. Then I heard the sound of scrubbing and putting things in order.

13
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.343
Later when I passed the room as I went to lunch, I saw that everything was restored to

14
00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:02.304
its proper place.

15
00:01:04.124 --> 00:01:07.547
Leah stood on the window seat, cleaning soot from the window.

16
00:01:08.608 --> 00:01:12.711
I was about to ask her what had happened because I wanted to hear what the servants had

17
00:01:12.731 --> 00:01:13.312
been told.

18
00:01:14.293 --> 00:01:18.356
But as I entered the room, I suddenly noticed a second woman.

19
00:01:19.457 --> 00:01:26.282
Grace Poole was sitting in a chair, sewing new curtains for the bed She was intent on her

20
00:01:26.362 --> 00:01:32.107
work, and her face showed none of the desperation I'd expect from someone who'd just tried to kill

21
00:01:32.127 --> 00:01:32.427
her master.

22
00:01:34.024 --> 00:01:34.885
I was amazed.

23
00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:36.466
Hadn't Mr.

24
00:01:36.546 --> 00:01:42.051
Rochester immediately gone up to the third floor to confront her and accuse her of attempted murder?

25
00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:44.894
And yet she sat here so coolly.

26
00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.856
She looked up while I still gazed at her.

27
00:01:47.876 --> 00:01:53.121
"Good morning, miss," she said in her usual brief way and went on sewing.

28
00:01:54.161 --> 00:01:55.443
I decided to test her.

29
00:01:55.463 --> 00:01:58.525
"Good morning, Grace," I replied.

30
00:01:58.545 --> 00:02:01.428
"Has anything happened here?

31
00:02:02.472 --> 00:02:05.273
I thought I heard the servants talking together a while ago."

32
00:02:05.293 --> 00:02:08.154
"Master was reading in bed last night.

33
00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:12.496
He fell asleep with his candle lit, and the bed curtains caught on fire.

34
00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:17.218
Fortunately he awoke in time and put out the flames with the water in his pitcher."

35
00:02:18.198 --> 00:02:18.879
I stared at her.

36
00:02:18.899 --> 00:02:20.459
"Did Mr.

37
00:02:20.559 --> 00:02:21.940
Rochester wake no one?

38
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.181
Did nobody hear him?"

39
00:02:25.181 --> 00:02:26.242
Grace raised her eyes.

40
00:02:26.262 --> 00:02:31.384
"The servants would be unlikely to hear because, as you know, their rooms are far away.

41
00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:37.954
Mrs. Fairfax's room and yours are the nearest to master's, but she's old and a heavy sleeper."

42
00:02:39.074 --> 00:02:44.976
She paused and said in a significant tone, "But you are young, miss, and I assume a light

43
00:02:45.056 --> 00:02:48.977
sleeper. Perhaps you heard something?"

44
00:02:49.957 --> 00:02:52.178
I lowered my voice so Leah couldn't hear me.

45
00:02:52.198 --> 00:02:55.619
"I'm certain I heard a strange laugh."

46
00:02:57.419 --> 00:02:59.220
Grace carefully threaded her needle.

47
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.042
"It's unlikely master would laugh when he was in such danger.

48
00:03:04.062 --> 00:03:05.223
You must have been dreaming."

49
00:03:05.243 --> 00:03:07.464
"I was not dreaming!"

50
00:03:07.824 --> 00:03:08.885
I said indignantly.

51
00:03:08.905 --> 00:03:13.007
"You didn't think of opening the door and looking out into the corridor?"

52
00:03:14.128 --> 00:03:19.011
She seemed to be cross-examining me, trying to trick me into giving her some information.

53
00:03:20.091 --> 00:03:24.694
I was afraid if she discovered that I knew what she'd done, she would try to harm me.

54
00:03:24.714 --> 00:03:27.956
"On the contrary, I locked my door."

55
00:03:29.144 --> 00:03:31.365
"That was a wise thing to do," she said.

56
00:03:31.385 --> 00:03:38.248
"I've never heard of thieves attempting to rob Thornfield, but everyone knows there are many valuables and very

57
00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:39.268
few servants here."

58
00:03:40.389 --> 00:03:44.150
We were interrupted by Mary, the cook, telling us that lunch was ready.

59
00:03:45.251 --> 00:03:49.232
Grace said that she would take hers upstairs, but I went down to join Mrs.

60
00:03:49.272 --> 00:03:54.694
Fairfax. I ate hardly anything because my mind was full of questions.

61
00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:56.575
Why had Mr.

62
00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.376
Rochester sworn me to secrecy?

63
00:03:59.464 --> 00:04:02.225
Why didn't he have Grace arrested for trying to kill him?

64
00:04:03.266 --> 00:04:05.107
What power did she hold over him?

65
00:04:06.127 --> 00:04:08.388
Had he once been romantically involved with her?

66
00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:10.629
But she was so plain.

67
00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:15.491
And yet, I reminded myself, I was plain and he seemed to favor me.

68
00:04:15.511 --> 00:04:19.653
I remembered his voice and the way he looked at me the night before.

69
00:04:20.794 --> 00:04:25.236
I passed the afternoon with Adele in the schoolroom, and I still expected to see Mr.

70
00:04:25.296 --> 00:04:29.997
Rochester. Our school day ended, and I wanted to talk to Mr.

71
00:04:30.037 --> 00:04:31.418
Rochester more than ever.

72
00:04:32.558 --> 00:04:34.859
I needed to ask him again about Grace Poole.

73
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:41.422
I knew the pleasure of alternately vexing and soothing him; it was one I delighted in and I

74
00:04:41.462 --> 00:04:43.163
was eager to engage in it now.

75
00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.805
At last someone knocked at my door.

76
00:04:47.845 --> 00:04:51.246
But it was only Leah, telling me that tea was ready in Mrs.

77
00:04:51.286 --> 00:04:52.267
Fairfax's room.

78
00:04:52.287 --> 00:04:55.693
"You must want your tea," said Mrs.

79
00:04:55.733 --> 00:04:57.414
Fairfax as she poured me a cup.

80
00:04:58.475 --> 00:05:01.558
"You ate hardly anything at lunch, and you look flushed."

81
00:05:01.578 --> 00:05:03.800
"Oh, I'm quite well!"

82
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:04.961
I protested.

83
00:05:04.981 --> 00:05:06.962
"I never felt better."

84
00:05:08.003 --> 00:05:09.905
Mrs. Fairfax looked out her window.

85
00:05:09.925 --> 00:05:14.349
"Mr. Rochester has had a favorable day for his journey."

86
00:05:14.369 --> 00:05:17.731
"Journey? I didn't know he was out."

87
00:05:17.751 --> 00:05:19.713
"Oh, yes."

88
00:05:20.914 --> 00:05:22.896
Mrs. Fairfax sat down at the table.

89
00:05:23.892 --> 00:05:26.356
"He set off first thing this morning for Mr.

90
00:05:26.496 --> 00:05:29.641
Eshton's place ten miles on the other side of Millcote.

91
00:05:30.762 --> 00:05:32.765
I believe there's quite a group assembled there.

92
00:05:33.806 --> 00:05:35.549
He's likely to stay a week or more."

93
00:05:35.569 --> 00:05:38.413
"Are there ladies at Mr.

94
00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:40.096
Eshton's?" I blurted out.

95
00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:48.367
"Mrs. Eshton and her daughters, very elegant ladies, and then there are Blanche and Mary Ingram, most beautiful

96
00:05:48.427 --> 00:05:49.108
women indeed.

97
00:05:49.608 --> 00:05:54.893
I last saw Blanche when she was 18 and came to a Christmas party here half a dozen

98
00:05:54.953 --> 00:05:55.634
years ago."

99
00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:57.616
"And what was she like?"

100
00:05:58.717 --> 00:05:59.878
I put down my teacup.

101
00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:06.164
Mrs. Fairfax went on to describe a tall and graceful young lady with black hair and eyes.

102
00:06:07.368 --> 00:06:12.270
"All the gentlemen admired her not only for her beauty but for her accomplishments.

103
00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.050
I remember that she and Mr.

104
00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.711
Rochester sang a duet.

105
00:06:17.871 --> 00:06:20.472
And when she sat down at the piano, Mr.

106
00:06:20.592 --> 00:06:23.333
Rochester said that she played remarkably well."

107
00:06:24.473 --> 00:06:27.234
I remembered his comments on my own musical talent.

108
00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:31.175
As I finished my tea, I wondered aloud if Mr.

109
00:06:31.255 --> 00:06:33.276
Rochester and Miss Ingram would marry.

110
00:06:34.956 --> 00:06:35.436
But Mrs.

111
00:06:35.496 --> 00:06:38.899
Fairfax thought it unlikely given the difference in their ages.

112
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.921
After tea I retired to my room.

113
00:06:41.941 --> 00:06:45.563
"Jane, you're a fool," I said to myself.

114
00:06:46.744 --> 00:06:48.705
"You are not a favorite of Mr.

115
00:06:48.806 --> 00:06:51.487
Rochester's. Open your eyes!

116
00:06:52.688 --> 00:06:57.772
It does no woman any good to be flattered by a superior who has no intention of marrying

117
00:06:57.832 --> 00:07:05.078
her." I sentenced myself to draw a self-portrait in chalk and to paint a fine likeness of Blanche,

118
00:07:05.398 --> 00:07:06.138
based on Mrs.

119
00:07:06.178 --> 00:07:07.419
Fairfax's description.

120
00:07:08.359 --> 00:07:14.381
My picture, which I labeled "Portrait of a poor, plain governess," took me only two hours the next

121
00:07:14.461 --> 00:07:23.384
day. I worked for days on the other portrait, which I titled "Blanche, an accomplished lady of rank."

122
00:07:23.404 --> 00:07:29.209
I was grateful for this exercise because without it I would have been unable to tolerate what happened

123
00:07:29.309 --> 00:07:29.610
next.
